}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the gating/back-out action when a shadow difference falls outside the approved delta allowlist (e.g. fail the shadow contract test and hold the cutover).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4","E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'record comparison mismatches without issuing duplicate model calls'","'report no differences outside the approved delta allowlist'","ABSENCE: no stated consequence/back-out when an unapproved difference is observed"],"finding":"The plan records shadow-comparison mismatches outside the approved delta allowlist but does not state what a non-allowlisted mismatch triggers (block the cutover, revert, or merely log), leaving the rollback/gating decision undefined.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4350037688dcdcd8","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('During expand-contract...') + AC7","norm_id":"nac64b96592d2ff21","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Shadow comparison surfaces an unapproved difference during expand-contract; the executor does not know whether to hold the cutover or proceed."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the shadow comparison fixes the observed call set to the NEW selection and derives the LEGACY verdict as a pure projection over that same set (never a legacy re-selection), and state how a unit the new path sheds/omits is represented in the legacy projection without issuing an extra call.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'compute the legacy and new deterministic projections from the same calls and record comparison mismatches without issuing duplicate model calls'","Approved deltas named in plan ('effective disable/retune, project DET inclusion, project applicability, explicit budget enforcement') are precisely the axes that change the ISSUED call set, so a single call set cannot be the output of both selection paths","Current path issues one agent call per included criterion (CodeReviewBatchRunner.run loops active_criteria); a legacy criterion the new path sheds would have no call in the shared set"],"finding":"The expand-contract shadow-comparison mechanism ('compute the legacy and new deterministic projections from the same calls and record comparison mismatches without issuing duplicate model calls') is under-specified: because the approved deltas (effective disable/retune, project DET inclusion, project applicability, budget shedding) each change WHICH criterion calls are issued, legacy and new SELECTION cannot both produce the one observed call set. The plan does not state that the observed call set is fixed to the new selection with the legacy verdict recomputed as a pure projection over that same set, nor how a unit the new path sheds/omits (never called) is represented in the legacy projection.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2471dda3f552c15","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, para 5 ('During expand-contract, compute the legacy and new deterministic projections from the same calls...') and AC line 7 ('Shadow contract tests use one observed call set...')","norm_id":"ne020fa6e0a5f4932","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A budget-shed unit: legacy would have called it, new sheds it — how does the legacy projection score a call that was never issued?","A project criterion non-applicable under new globs but unconditionally run under legacy fan-in"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the harness records the NEW-selection call set once, then computes both the legacy and new deterministic verdicts as projections over that single set — treating a new-path-shed/omitted unit as an approved-delta difference in the legacy projection rather than re-issuing its call.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_thresho